    <!-- Renamed in Task 19: "feel it on its own" became the test call, and the
        name matters — a test call plays exactly what a call plays, through the
        same route, so on Silent it stays silent and the test never lies. -->
    <string name="ready_feel">Feel a test call</string>
    <string name="ready_stop">Stop</string>

    <!-- The comparison button. "Is it strong enough?" cannot be answered against
         a memory of the stock buzz, so this plays the real thing beside it. The
         pattern is the one this phone actually uses, read off `dumpsys
         vibrator_manager` rather than copied from AOSP: one second at full
         amplitude, then one second of complete silence, repeating. -->
    <string name="ready_stock">Play the phone\'s own buzz</string>
    <string name="ready_stock_stop">Stop the buzz</string>
    <string name="ready_stock_help">The vibration Android uses for a call on this phone: one
        second at full strength, then one second of silence. Play it, then play yours, and
        compare the two.</string>

