    <!-- Setup. Task 9, and it is short on purpose: the supersede measurement
         (PROFILE.md §11 R2) removed almost everything this screen was going to
         ask for. What is left is the one setting that silently kills the app.

         The verdict is read live from the phone's ringer mode, so this is the
         only guidance there is — and "silent" is the case that matters, because
         to anyone who is not thinking about it, silent and vibrate are both just
         "no sound". -->
    <string name="setup_wont_title">Won\'t work yet</string>


    <string name="setup_ring_on">Your phone is on ring, so a call plays this song and Thrum vibrates to it.</string>

    <string name="setup_silent">Your phone is on silent, and Android throws the vibration away
        before it reaches the motor. No app can get around that.</string>
    <string name="setup_silent_help">It has to be Vibrate, not Silent. Both look like \"no sound\",
        but Silent means nothing vibrates at all.</string>
    <string name="setup_sound_action">Open sound settings</string>

    <string name="setup_ring_off">Your phone is on ring and your ringtone is a different sound, so Thrum stays quiet rather than play one song over another.</string>
    <string name="setup_ring_off_help">Set this song as your ringtone, or put your phone on vibrate.</string>

    <string name="setup_unknown">Thrum can\'t read this phone\'s ringer setting, so it can\'t
        promise anything either way. It will still try when a call comes in.</string>

    <!-- Tune the feel. Task 24, screen 15. Rebuilt 2026-10-06 after Mutalib said he
